{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_08de510213784991acff3a7ddfd2d26a1bf56dcfd722e924b8530389771b4057"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"angles serve starts an embedded axum HTTP server on 127.0.0.1:8080 exposing /health, /api/config, /api/providers, and /api/chat for a browser-based web console."},{"claim_ids":["clm_137c25aa3f9fb19b5e4975bee4ee14fe17e75143af74ac53b8d4a4e5ef77ce0f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the repo includes a release workflow (.github/workflows/release.yml), a Cross.toml for cross-compilation, and a docs/ directory published as a GitHub Pages site."},{"claim_ids":["clm_195c7c2307fe68aa29cb4f2fdea4ace41a70c590cac5f7e9760dcf3f4e0696be"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The CLI offers subcommands including an interactive default session (angles), angles exec for one-shot runs, angles plan, angles serve, angles gateway, angles config, angles doctor, and angles help."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2c1b59e55b0b0464c09ba4fd8aee189e3548ef39726834691ab3c5420394c13f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tool ships as a single static ~1.6 MB Rust binary with zero runtime dependencies (no Node, Python, or dynamic libc), aimed at constrained environments like ARM64 SBCs, rootless containers, and iSH."},{"claim_ids":["clm_41f06f5f6f6ba41e44dff6c443f3e2f8072039013482bd8e80437725096bb408"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"All agent capabilities are exposed as curated angles-* commands rather than free-form shell improvisation, binding the model to a deterministic tool set."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4d4d807e141d1bd3d70afcd9edfa68e1404cea81c818e12ae4ee31dd82c2ce34"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Configuration persists at ~/.angles/config.json with fields for language, provider, base_url, wire_api, model, max_tokens, daily token budget, agent persona, search engine, and approval policy; API keys can come from ANGLES_API_KEY and are not sent through a relay."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5980932033004b1dda83155dc8829566ea84800f8f8e395219b104048a36bfdd"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The 13 KB instructions.txt system-prompt template uses handlebars-style {{variable}} injection for config values, persona, and architecture, and directs the agent to emit operation plans with fixed verbs before non-trivial tasks."},{"claim_ids":["clm_96d7777be6e1d4b437721b14c8e7fe3f84ad6bc56be5017ef3269c91c739fe41"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The codebase is organized into Rust modules including main.rs (entry/routing), cli.rs, config.rs, provider.rs, gateway.rs, instructions.rs, api.rs, search.rs, server.rs, and tools.rs, plus instructions.txt, providers.toml, and docs/."},{"claim_ids":["clm_b6fc85dcc26bb20d936a881ee7d164ce4beef12e2b683f6c8008e14e2fdc4c92"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"A provider registry (provider.rs plus providers.toml) maps 11 providers to three wire protocols — OpenAI Chat Completions, Anthropic Messages, or Gemini Native — normalizing streaming and tool calls so the rest of the code is provider-agnostic."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d2dbc13f5fe6943e4a298d68ed6d0e8738d4d7469348c0164edfa72109819ae6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The conversation loop lives in api.rs, an OpenAI/Anthropic/Gemini client with streaming and a tool-calling loop that resolves angles-* commands to implementations in tools.rs."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d6957ea3dca3e0cd895169a043349e6a546e9b7e24b0d1aabfe86c3b58f6efe0"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The safety model: reads need no approval, writes follow the configured approval policy, and deletions or dangerous operations always require user confirmation."},{"claim_ids":["clm_fbafde5fea1c06a8cf683e708f50dd842c8a351975b61be09d7ce184f9b2c7c1"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: building from source uses cargo build --release with Makefile targets for Linux ARM64/x64 and macOS ARM64 cross-compilation, and GitHub Actions produces prebuilt binaries for all 5 platforms on every tag push."}],"claim_ids":["clm_08de510213784991acff3a7ddfd2d26a1bf56dcfd722e924b8530389771b4057","clm_137c25aa3f9fb19b5e4975bee4ee14fe17e75143af74ac53b8d4a4e5ef77ce0f","clm_195c7c2307fe68aa29cb4f2fdea4ace41a70c590cac5f7e9760dcf3f4e0696be","clm_2c1b59e55b0b0464c09ba4fd8aee189e3548ef39726834691ab3c5420394c13f","clm_41f06f5f6f6ba41e44dff6c443f3e2f8072039013482bd8e80437725096bb408","clm_4d4d807e141d1bd3d70afcd9edfa68e1404cea81c818e12ae4ee31dd82c2ce34","clm_5980932033004b1dda83155dc8829566ea84800f8f8e395219b104048a36bfdd","clm_96d7777be6e1d4b437721b14c8e7fe3f84ad6bc56be5017ef3269c91c739fe41","clm_b6fc85dcc26bb20d936a881ee7d164ce4beef12e2b683f6c8008e14e2fdc4c92","clm_d2dbc13f5fe6943e4a298d68ed6d0e8738d4d7469348c0164edfa72109819ae6","clm_d6957ea3dca3e0cd895169a043349e6a546e9b7e24b0d1aabfe86c3b58f6efe0","clm_fbafde5fea1c06a8cf683e708f50dd842c8a351975b61be09d7ce184f9b2c7c1"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:35:15Z","created_by_operation":"op_4351f93141a34092bdfa567d49d41262","id":"pg_01ca5da827305c90add8520ce4b15b00","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/angleschina-angles-cli-readme-md-53cf51b702e4-520ce4b15b00.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_aeaab04e90e45dc8b5b3007da6ae6ef3"],"title":"angleschina/angles-cli/README.md @ 53cf51b702e4","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:35:15Z","updated_by_operation":"op_4351f93141a34092bdfa567d49d41262"}
